---
import AppLayout from '../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/app.css';
import '../styles/page.css';

const updated = 'August 2026';
const supportEmail = 'yash@typethink.ai';
---

<AppLayout
	title="Privacy Policy — doodlebooth.lol"
	description="What data doodlebooth.lol stores, where it comes from, who processes it, and how to get a doodle removed."
>
	<Navbar />

	<main class="page">
		<div class="page-hero">
			<div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
			<h1>Privacy <span class="grad">Policy</span></h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Short version: no accounts, no ad pixels, and nothing sold. We use one analytics tool,
				we store the doodles you submit to the wall, and we delete them on request.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="prose">
			<p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {updated}</p>

			<h2>The short version</h2>
			<div class="facts">
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Accounts</div><div class="v">None — no signup or login</div></div>
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Cookies</div><div class="v">Analytics only</div></div>
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Ad pixels</div><div class="v">None</div></div>
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Payments</div><div class="v">None — the site is free</div></div>
				<div class="fact"><div class="k">Selling data</div><div class="v">Never</div></div>
			</div>

			<h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
			<p>
				We use <a href="https://datafa.st" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DataFast</a>
				to understand how people find and use the site — which pages get visited and which
				sources send traffic. It records things like the page viewed, the referring source, and
				general device, browser and country-level information.
			</p>
			<p>
				DataFast <strong>sets cookies</strong> to recognise a returning visitor so those numbers
				aren't wildly inflated. That is the only cookie-based tracking on the site. We do not run
				advertising pixels, we are not part of an ad network, and we never sell or share this
				data. You can block or clear these cookies in your browser settings at any time; the site
				works fine without them. See
				<a href="https://datafa.st/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DataFast's privacy policy</a>
				for how they handle it as our processor.
			</p>

			<h2>What we store</h2>
			<p>
				When you drop a doodle on the wall, we save the following:
			</p>
			<ul class="steps">
				<li><b>The drawing</b> — the image you created in the booth, copied to our own storage.</li>
				<li><b>A caption or title</b>, if you added one.</li>
				<li><b>Timestamps</b> for when the doodle was submitted.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				We do not collect email addresses, phone numbers, names, or anything behind a login,
				because there is no login. A doodle is only ever what you chose to draw and submit.
			</p>

			<h2>Where it comes from</h2>
			<p>
				Everything on the wall is drawn by visitors in the booth. We don't import content from
				other services or scrape anything from elsewhere.
			</p>

			<h2>Who processes it</h2>
			<ul class="steps">
				<li><b>Cloudflare</b> — hosting, database and image storage.</li>
				<li><b>DataFast</b> — website analytics.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Local storage on your device</h2>
			<p>
				Aside from the analytics cookies described above, we store a single value in your
				browser's local storage, <strong>doodlebooth-theme</strong>, to remember whether you
				chose light or dark mode. It is not an identifier, it never leaves your device, and
				clearing your browser data removes it.
			</p>

			<h2>Server logs</h2>
			<p>
				Our host processes standard request data such as IP address and user agent to serve
				traffic and block abuse. We do not build profiles from it or use it for advertising.
			</p>

			<h2>Getting a doodle removed</h2>
			<div class="callout">
				<p>
					Email <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a> and we will delete the
					doodle and its stored image. No account verification hoops, no explanation required.
				</p>
			</div>

			<h2>Children</h2>
			<p>
				This site is not directed at children. If you believe a minor has submitted something
				that should be removed, email us and we will take it down promptly.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				If this policy changes, the date at the top will change with it.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Privacy questions or removal requests:
				<a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="page-cta">
			<a href="/">Back to the wall</a>
		</div>
	</main>

	<Footer />

	<script>
		import { initThemeToggle } from '../lib/theme';
		const themeToggle = document.getElementById('themeToggle');
		if (themeToggle) initThemeToggle(themeToggle);
	</script>
</AppLayout>
